{
  "title": { "en": "Two directions" },
  "tray": "proof",
  "intro": [
    {
      "t": {
        "en": "In the truth circuits, the ↔ of <level-ref to=\"g-iff\"></level-ref> meant true together and false together. In the kernel, A ↔ B is “(A → B) ∧ (B → A)”: the → holds both ways."
      }
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "iffUse_1",
      "kind": "proof",
      "step": { "en": "One direction" },
      "tests": [{ "premises": { "p": "A ↔ B", "q": "A" }, "goal": "B" }],
      "cases": [{ "A": "Sat", "B": "Rest" }, { "A": "Coffee", "B": "Awake" }],
      "hint": [
        {
          "en": "<part-ref to=\"part:andE\"></part-ref> splits ↔ too: into the two “if … then …”s; use the right one."
        }
      ],
      "solution": ["e = andE(p)", "m = mp(e.left, q)", "goal <- m"]
    },
    {
      "id": "iffUse_2",
      "kind": "proof",
      "step": { "en": "The other direction" },
      "tests": [{ "premises": { "p": "A ↔ B", "q": "¬A" }, "goal": "¬B" }],
      "cases": [{ "A": "Sat", "B": "Rest" }, { "A": "Coffee", "B": "Awake" }],
      "hint": [
        {
          "en": "This time it takes the other direction: assume “I rest” and see whether it runs into a contradiction."
        }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "f = impI[A=B](body: m2) {",
        "  body {",
        "    m1 = mp(e.right, f.body)",
        "    m2 = mp(q, m1)",
        "  }",
        "}",
        "e = andE(p)",
        "goal <- f"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
